{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.PhysicalIntractability","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.PhysicalIntractability","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Normed"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qou_physical_intractability_unconditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qou_physical_intractability_unconditional","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PhysicalIntractability.lean#L212-L224","doc":"**QOU physical intractability — UNCONDITIONAL (sorry-free).**  The only\nremaining hypothesis is the *physical model*: a bandwidth-`B` device that\ncorrectly extracts the full surviving `3^{3n}`-leaf resolution tree accesses\n`≤ steps n · B` bits.  Given that, its step count is super-polynomial — **no\nbandwidth-limited device decides the boundary problem in polynomial time.**\nThe exponential-domination fact is now discharged (`superPoly_two_pow`);\nthe information requirement `3^{3n}` is derived from the tree.  Scope:\nbandwidth-limited computation — strictly weaker than abstract `P ≠ NP`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qou_physical_intractability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qou_physical_intractability","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PhysicalIntractability.lean#L193-L210","doc":"**QOU physical intractability (sorry-free, conditional on the two named\ninputs).**  For the non-torsion substrate, if a bandwidth-`B` device\ncorrectly extracts the full surviving `3^{3n}`-leaf resolution tree for the\nboundary family, then — given the standard fact that `2^n` dominates every\npolynomial — its step count is super-polynomial: **no bandwidth-limited\ndevice decides the boundary problem in polynomial time.**\n\nThe `info(n) = 3^{3n}` requirement is *derived* here from the resolution\ntree (the QOU physical content); `exp_dominates_poly` is the standard\nexponential-domination fact (Mathlib-dischargeable; bean `qou-*`).  Scope\nremains bandwidth-limited computation — strictly weaker than abstract\n`P ≠ NP`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.two_pow_le_resolutionTreeSize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.two_pow_le_resolutionTreeSize","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PhysicalIntractability.lean#L185-L191","doc":"`2^n ≤ 3^{3n}` (sorry-free): the surviving tree of the size-`n` boundary\ninstance (`c = 3n`) dominates `2^n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.resolutionTreeSize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.resolutionTreeSize","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PhysicalIntractability.lean#L181-L183","doc":"The skein **resolution-tree size** of a `c`-crossing link: `3^c` leaves\n(three skein channels per crossing; in the non-torsion regime none cancel). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.steps_superPoly_of_info","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.steps_superPoly_of_info","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PhysicalIntractability.lean#L153-L167","doc":"**Division-free step lower bound (sorry-free).**  Cleaner than going\nthrough `info / B`: if `info n ≤ steps n * B` and `info` is\nsuper-polynomial, so is `steps` — cancel the constant `B` by scaling the\npolynomial witness.  This avoids `Nat`-division artifacts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.no_poly_bandwidth_decider_of_exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.no_poly_bandwidth_decider_of_exp","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PhysicalIntractability.lean#L140-L151","doc":"**Exponential information ⇒ physical intractability (sorry-free).**  The\nconcrete QOU case: if deciding size-`n` instances requires (per bandwidth\nunit) at least the `2^n` bits of the full degree-0 obstruction, and `2^n`\nitself is super-polynomial, then no bandwidth-limited device is\npolynomial-time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SuperPolynomial.of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SuperPolynomial.of_le","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PhysicalIntractability.lean#L126-L136","doc":"**Super-polynomiality lifts through a lower bound (sorry-free).**  If\n`g ≤ f` pointwise and `g` is super-polynomial, so is `f`.\n\nLives in the `SuperPolynomial` namespace so that generalized field\nnotation (`hg.of_le hle`) resolves: dot notation looks up\n`SuperPolynomial.of_le` on the head constant, and falls through to the\nunfolded pi-type (`Function.of_le`, which does not exist) if the lemma\nsits in the ambient `QOU.Information` namespace instead. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.no_poly_bandwidth_decider","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.no_poly_bandwidth_decider","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PhysicalIntractability.lean#L108-L122","doc":"**Physical intractability (sorry-free).**  If the information required to\ndecide `L` (per bandwidth unit, `info n / B`) is super-polynomial, then the\nstep count of *any* correct bandwidth-`B` device is super-polynomial too —\ni.e. no bandwidth-limited device decides `L` in polynomial time.\n\nA **derived** lower bound (pigeonhole on the bandwidth bound), not a fiat.\nScope: bandwidth-limited computation only — strictly weaker than abstract\n`P ≠ NP`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.superPoly_two_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.superPoly_two_pow","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PhysicalIntractability.lean#L78-L106","doc":"**`2^n` is super-polynomial (sorry-free).**  The standard \"exponential\ndominates every polynomial\" fact, discharged from Mathlib's little-o\n(`isLittleO_pow_const_const_pow_of_one_lt`).  Makes the QOU\nphysical-intractability theorem below *unconditional*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SuperPolynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SuperPolynomial","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PhysicalIntractability.lean#L66-L75","doc":"A function `f : ℕ → ℕ` is **super-polynomial** if it exceeds every\npolynomial `c · n^k` at some argument `n ≥ 1`.\n\nThe `1 ≤ n` guard is essential: without it the `n = 0` term `c · 0^k = 0`\n(for `k ≥ 1`) is `< f 0` for *any* `f` with `f 0 ≥ 1`, so a mere polynomial\nlike `n ↦ (n+1)^2` would spuriously satisfy the predicate (confirmed in Lean,\nbean `qou-qgyw`). Guarding the witness away from `0` makes the predicate mean\ngenuine polynomial domination and makes `PolyGrowth ⟹ ¬SuperPolynomial`\n(`PolyGrowthAlgebra.not_superPolynomial_of_polyGrowth`) provable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.steps_lower_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.steps_lower_bound","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PhysicalIntractability.lean#L56-L64","doc":"**Steps lower bound (sorry-free).**  A bandwidth-`B` device that in\n`steps n` steps accesses at most `steps n * B` bits, and is *correct*\n(accesses at least the `info n` bits needed to decide instance size `n`),\nmust run for at least `info n / B` steps. ","signatureChunk":0}]}